 {"question" "q-102994" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "x(t)=\\frac{1}{16}(2+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t))"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037927/state.json" "file_sha256" "37d51446b8b92ec0cad35ec3abeb6288a39eca6691a2b98cd6a918996197fd05" "basis" 1282 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037927/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-102994" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "x(t)=\\frac{1}{16}(2-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t))"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037927/state.json" "file_sha256" "37d51446b8b92ec0cad35ec3abeb6288a39eca6691a2b98cd6a918996197fd05" "basis" 1282 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037927/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-102994" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x(t)=\\frac{1}{16}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t))"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037927/state.json" "file_sha256" "37d51446b8b92ec0cad35ec3abeb6288a39eca6691a2b98cd6a918996197fd05" "basis" 1282 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037927/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-351551" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with velocity $v(t)=8{t}^{3}+12,$ where $t>0$ is the time. If the particle is at the position $x=10$ when $t=1,$ calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t.$\n\n$x(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039392/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe9a1332c42989973308ddf8886314d80182e2e5d081f01608a566c1cfcca93c"} {"question" "q-351551" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We start by integrating the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (8{t}^{3}+12)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{{t}^{4}}{4}+12t+C \\\\  & =2{t}^{4}+12t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $x(1)=10.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & =2(1)^{4}+12(1)+C \\\\ 10 & =2+12+C \\\\ C & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)=2{t}^{4}+12t-4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039392/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe9a1332c42989973308ddf8886314d80182e2e5d081f01608a566c1cfcca93c"} {"question" "q-351551" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039392/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e5ae4214e2b56e7613b0ac8b09ac5ca023e4bd8f79ce046113831d99933297e9"} {"question" "q-351551" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039392/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe9a1332c42989973308ddf8886314d80182e2e5d081f01608a566c1cfcca93c"} {"question" "q-351551" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2t^4+12t-4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039392/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe9a1332c42989973308ddf8886314d80182e2e5d081f01608a566c1cfcca93c"} {"question" "q-351556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with velocity $v(t)=\\frac{6}{t},$ where $t>0$ is the time. If the particle is at the position $x=4$ when $t=1,$ calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t.$\n\n$x(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039392/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe9a1332c42989973308ddf8886314d80182e2e5d081f01608a566c1cfcca93c"} {"question" "q-351556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We start by integrating the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{6}{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $x(1)=4.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)+C \\\\ 4 & =6(0)+C \\\\ C & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)=6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)+4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039392/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe9a1332c42989973308ddf8886314d80182e2e5d081f01608a566c1cfcca93c"} {"question" "q-351556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039392/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e5ae4214e2b56e7613b0ac8b09ac5ca023e4bd8f79ce046113831d99933297e9"} {"question" "q-351556" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039392/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe9a1332c42989973308ddf8886314d80182e2e5d081f01608a566c1cfcca93c"} {"question" "q-351556" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6\\ln(t)+4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039392/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe9a1332c42989973308ddf8886314d80182e2e5d081f01608a566c1cfcca93c"} {"question" "q-7287" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with velocity $v(t)=\\frac{{t}^{2}-t}{4},$ where $t>0$ is the time. If the particle is at the position $x=-\\frac{1}{6}$ when $t=2,$ calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039392/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe9a1332c42989973308ddf8886314d80182e2e5d081f01608a566c1cfcca93c"} {"question" "q-7287" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We start by integrating the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{{t}^{2}-t}{4})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{t}^{3}-\\frac{1}{8}{t}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C,$ we use the fact that $x(2)=-\\frac{1}{6}.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{6} & =\\frac{1}{12}(2)^{3}-\\frac{1}{8}(2)^{2}+C \\\\ -\\frac{1}{6} & =\\frac{1}{6}+C \\\\ C & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{1}{12}{t}^{3}-\\frac{1}{8}{t}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039392/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe9a1332c42989973308ddf8886314d80182e2e5d081f01608a566c1cfcca93c"} {"question" "q-7287" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "c